From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:55:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] DRMHelpers: Define the MediaTek modifiers for older
 libdrm

The MediaTek format modifiers are in the kernel's drm_fourcc.h, but not
in the libdrm copy that Kodi includes on Debian trixie (2.4.124). Define
the vendor and the 16L32 tile modifier when they are missing, so code
checking for them is not silently compiled out.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 xbmc/utils/DRMHelpers.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/DRMHelpers.h b/xbmc/utils/DRMHelpers.h
index dcc7f502f3..4cd8ff670c 100644
--- a/xbmc/utils/DRMHelpers.h
+++ b/xbmc/utils/DRMHelpers.h
@@ -11,6 +11,16 @@
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 
+#include <drm_fourcc.h>
+
+// missing from older libdrm copies of drm_fourcc.h (2.4.124 in Debian trixie)
+#ifndef DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_MTK
+#define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_MTK 0x0b
+#endif
+#ifndef DRM_FORMAT_MOD_MTK_16L_32S_TILE
+#define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_MTK_16L_32S_TILE fourcc_mod_code(MTK, 0x1)
+#endif
+
 namespace DRMHELPERS
 {
 
